  "rules": [
    "a name: 1 to 32 of a-z 0-9 _, the first a letter, no __, not ending in _; lowercase only on chain; the numbers (+0 ...) are gone from the v15 genesis and parse as nothing",
    "reserved names: salarium salt work admin support help official security wallet bank pool operator treasury exchange faucet explorer system root null, and every name starting with salarium",
    "name prices in SALT by length 1..7, then 8 and longer: 100000 25000 5000 1000 250 100 50 10 (the price rule of protocol versions 1 and 2; from version 3 the starting bid of a name's auction)",
    "short names (1-4 characters) are minted with the secret of a commit taken 600 to 86400 slots before (versions 1 and 2; MintHandle is refused from version 3)",
    "auctions (version 3): BidHandle's value is the bid; a bid on a free name opens the auction at its starting bid or more, ends = opened + 5 * E slots for an epoch of E slots (432000 on the main network: five days); a raise is at least bid + ceil(bid * 5 / 100) and not by the leader, and the beaten bid goes back; a bid taken at slot s sets ends = max(ends, s + max(1, floor(E / 24))) (3600 on the main network: an hour); the first beacon block with slot >= ends settles it (at most 1000 a block, the earliest end first): the leader holds the name, the bid splits as a mint's price",
    "a holder's auction (version 3, 21-names §4b): AuctionHandle {handle, start, step_bp, duration, extension}, amount 0, by the name's holder, of a name bound to no app and not on auction (or on its own auction without a bid, whose terms and time it replaces); start >= 1 SALT (holder_min_start), step_bp 100..=5000, duration E..=30 * E slots, extension 0..=E; a listing ends; ends = opened + duration; the first bid is at least start, a later one at least bid + max(1, ceil(bid * step_bp / 10000)), never by the holder nor the leader; a bid taken at slot s sets ends = max(ends, s + extension); while on auction no ListHandle, TransferHandle, ReleaseHandle or BindHandle; the first beacon block with slot >= ends hands the name to the leader as a sale (the holder's primary cleared, minted kept) and pays the holder the bid less the 5% royalty, which splits as a sale's; with no bid it expires and the name stays; CancelAuction {handle} by the holder before the first bid and before the end",
    "commit hash = derive \"Salarium handle commit v1\" of borsh(handle) ‖ sender account id ‖ 32-byte secret",
    "bids bound to their auction (protocol version 5, 21-names §4b): BidAuction {handle, terms: [u8; 32]}, its value the bid, is taken only on a live auction of handle whose terms hash is terms, as BidHandle raises one (escrow, the beaten bid back, the extension); otherwise it fails with its value back, and it never opens an auction; from version 5 BidHandle on a holder's auction fails with its value back (it still opens and raises a new name's); terms hash = derive \"Salarium auction terms v1\" of borsh(handle) ‖ borsh(seller: Option<account id>: 0, or 1 ‖ 20 bytes; none for a new name's auction) ‖ opened u64 LE ‖ scheduled u64 LE ‖ start u64 LE ‖ step_bp u16 LE ‖ extension u64 LE — the auction's fields as handle_get writes them (`terms`); ends, the leader, the bid and the count are not terms",
    "borsh(Handle): tag 0 Name(String) (tag 1, the numbers', decodes as nothing); HandleKind: u8 0 name",
    "registry calls (action tag 1 {call, amount}), paid in SALT: CommitHandle 23 {hash}, MintHandle 24 {handle, secret: Option<[u8;32]>}, TransferHandle 25 {handle, to}, SetPrimary 26 {handle}, ClearPrimary 27 {kind}, ReleaseHandle 28 {handle}, ListHandle 29 {handle, price: u64}, UnlistHandle 30 {handle}, BuyHandle 31 {handle}, BindHandle 35 {handle, slug: Option<String>} (24-app-studio §2: the holder points it at a live grain it owns, or clears it with none; a transfer, a sale or a release clears it, and so does retiring the grain), BidHandle 60 {handle} (version 3), AuctionHandle 61 {handle, start: u64, step_bp: u16, duration: u64, extension: u64} (version 3), CancelAuction 62 {handle} (version 3), BidAuction 75 {handle, terms: [u8; 32]} (version 5)",
    "a sale's royalty is 5% of the price, rounded down; 10% of a mint and of a royalty go to the future payments fund, the rest to the service treasury",
    "display: @name"
  ],
